Task: bounded implementation advice for Rust migration, no tools/writes/acceptance. Root owns source edits. Diagnose and propose minimal exact edits (not full copies) to make historical CLI/HTTP mission status readable for a completed worker whose nonmanaged planned task is blocked with no current review. Real retained public recovery fixture currently returns mission-status-planning-unported. The actual scopes are waiting/ready. Need real report attribution observation, not fabricated empty facts. Strict historical JSON contract applies. Compare supplied Go provenReport and result branch with existing Rust task_reports and pure consumer. Do not reuse automatic relay as display proof: it reads agent cwd, requires consent and stronger content checks; status is read-only. Preserve review precedence, completed submitted/accepted behavior, unknown IO/cleanup causes, no hidden clock margin. Existing saved report_timestamp_skew_seconds may be consumed only if it matches the actual Go producer. Exclude incomplete-delivery branch if its evidence is not supplied, with explicit remaining refusal; do not bypass safety. Return <=1800 words: (1) exact missing contracts and narrow eligible shape, (2) concrete Rust helper and call-site patch proposal with docstrings/errors, (3) 5 discriminating tests incl missing/stale/ambiguous reports, (4) context gaps and uncertain assumptions. No claim of tests run. Provenance/worker-completion recovery is already locally verified, and this task grants no launch, mutation, acceptance, install or publication.

